==================================================
ANTI-FAILURE RULES
==================================================

NEVER include:
- children, babies, toddlers, kids
- faces (only hands and objects)
- cartoon or animated style
- mascots or characters with faces
- dialogue or voiceover
- text overlays
- multiple scenes or cuts

PHYSICS RULE (CRITICAL — videos must look real):
- Gravity works normally (things fall down, liquids pour down)
- Liquids behave like real liquids (honey is thick and slow, water splashes)
- Objects have real weight (heavy things don't float, light things don't thud)
- Cutting requires force (knife presses through, not magically splits)
- Steam rises UP, smoke drifts, dust settles DOWN
- Surfaces react realistically (bread compresses under knife, clay deforms under pressure)
- No impossible physics: nothing floats without support, nothing moves without cause
- Describe the PHYSICAL INTERACTION clearly so Veo renders correct physics
- Example: "knife slowly presses through crispy bread crust, crumbs fall onto cutting board" (gravity + force + result)

ALWAYS include:
- photorealistic quality
- real textures and materials
- crisp ASMR sounds (no music)
- one satisfying action
- warm natural lighting
- shallow depth of field
- physically accurate motion and interactions

Generate COMPLETELY NEW satisfying scene each time. Never repeat. Rotate categories. Pure JSON only.
```
